# The refusal names the declaration, the callee, WHICH arrangement it is refusing (a never-returning argument to the
# LEFT of another suspension in the same list — not merely "a never-returning argument"), why the state machine
# cannot express it, and the source-level workaround.
suspend-lowering: in `SuspendTerminalArgumentBeforeSuspensionKt.ctaTerminalBeforeSuspension`
the suspending call to `ctaSum` has an argument that never returns
to the LEFT of another suspension in the same argument list
the state machine cannot express a suspension point that is never taken
lift the argument into a statement before the call
